    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0495" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/5–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Baruch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-19T00:00:00+02:00">May 19,
                            1945—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received May 19—6:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1089. Embtel 990, May 7, noon.…<anchor n="9a" xml:id="d352-f1"/> has again been
                    approached by DNB representative … who stated that Inouye, Japanese Counselor
                    here, inquired whether there had been any results following … last approach.</p>
                <p>We have informed … that when he next sees … he should inform Inouye that unless
                    Inouye is (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) acting under instructions, (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) can produce satisfactory evidence of his
                    authority and (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) is prepared to propose
                    unconditional surrender, no further contact with … on this subject is desired.…
                    may add that we do not propose to act as channel for transmission of Japanese
                    propaganda to Washington.</p>
                <p>My British and Chinese colleagues have been apprised of foregoing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baruch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
